    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) and **Gabriel Moreno** (70.65), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable date with Miles Mikolas. **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine today; his elite speed profile combined with Mikolas\u2019s slow delivery creates a high-probability environment for stolen bases, a category we are prioritizing heavily. **Austin Riley** (70.38) also grades out as an elite start, as his projection is bolstered by a massive +16% park factor and a favorable matchup against Shane Baz. While the lineup remains technically pending, these anchors provide the high-ceiling production required to chase our 5x5 targets.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision landed on **Josh Naylor** (49.47), who narrowly missed the cut behind the stability of **Vinnie Pasquantino** (53.47). Despite **Josh Naylor** offering a solid baseline, the optimizer preferred **Vinnie Pasquantino**\u2019s positional flexibility and slightly higher base projection, even while acknowledging the tougher matchup against Framber Valdez. We are also closely monitoring **Jose Caballero** (51.08) and **Mickey Moniak** (49.72); while they hold starting roles today, their scores are suppressed by high-skill opposing arms (Cristopher S\u00e1nchez and Jacob Misiorowski, respectively). **Jose Caballero** remains a necessary evil for his speed, but we must accept the lower floor against S\u00e1nchez\u2019s sub-3.00 xERA.\n\nRisks persist across the board as the majority of our lineup is currently \"Lineup Pending.\" Specifically, **Brice Turang** (57.94) is trending toward a marginal start due to the lefty-on-lefty disadvantage against Kyle Freeland, which tempers our expectations for his counting stats. Meanwhile, the bench remains deep but static, with players like **Edwin Arroyo** (45.76) and **Travis Bazzana** (40.58) available if last-minute scratches occur. We have effectively balanced our need for sprint-speed contributors with our park-adjusted power hitters, provided that the confirmed lineups align with our current assumptions for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, and **James Wood**.",
